---
import Availability from '../../components/Availability.astro';
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
import Type from '../../components/Type.astro';
import PokemonImage from '../../components/PokemonImage.astro';
import AbilityLink from '../../components/AbilityLink.astro';
import { species, abilities, abilityAlias, url, hasDocumentedSource, availabilityToken, STAT_NAMES } from '../../lib/data';
const types = [...new Set(species.flatMap(s => s.types))].sort();
const regions = [...new Set(species.map((s) => s.region))];
---
<StarlightPage frontmatter={{ title: 'Pokémon', description: 'Every Pokémon in Origin HeartGold: types, abilities, base stats and how to get it.', tableOfContents: false }}>
	<p>Find Pokémon by type, ability or availability, then open a page for stats, evolution, moves and locations. All {species.length} Pokémon and forms are listed, including battle-only forms and those unavailable through normal play. “No known way to get it” means a way to obtain that Pokémon is not known.</p>
	<p><a href={url('/calendar/')}>Browse calendar encounters</a> · <a href={url('/mechanics/#held-item-forms')}>Held-item transformations</a></p>
	<div class="table-filter" data-table="mon-table">
		<input type="search" placeholder="Search by name, type or ability…" aria-label="Search Pokémon" />
    <select data-key="type" aria-label="Pokémon type"><option value="">All types</option>{types.map(t => <option>{t}</option>)}</select>
    <select data-key="ability" aria-label="Pokémon ability"><option value="">All abilities (regular or hidden)</option>{abilities.map(a => <option value={a.id}>{a.name}{abilityAlias(a) ? ` (${abilityAlias(a)} — author alias)` : ''}</option>)}</select>
		<select data-key="region" aria-label="Region">
			<option value="">All Pokédex ranges</option>
			{regions.map((r) => <option value={r}>{r}</option>)}
		</select>
		<select data-key="availability" aria-label="Availability">
			<option value="">All availability</option>
			<option value="documented">Where to get it</option>
			<option value="battle">Battle only</option>
			<option value="unavailable">NOT AVAILABLE IN GAME</option>
			<option value="unknown">No known way to get it</option>
		</select>
		<span class="filter-count" aria-live="polite"></span>
	</div>
	<p>Base stats come from this hack’s ROM. Select a stat heading to sort lowest first; select it again for highest first. BST is the total of all six stats. Scroll sideways to see every column.</p>
	<p class="small">Planning for a gym? <a href={url('/guide/ecruteak-olivine/#olivine-gym-jasmines-rule-three-pokémon-with-base-defense-130')}>Jasmine’s Defense rule</a> also checks a fixed species list, with exceptions explained in the guide.</p>
	<table id="mon-table" class="sortable compact">
		<thead><tr><th data-sort-type="number">Species / form</th><th>Pokémon</th><th>Type</th><th>Abilities</th><th>Hidden</th><th class="base-stat" data-sort-type="number">BST</th>{STAT_NAMES.map(name => <th class="base-stat" data-sort-type="number">{name}</th>)}<th>Availability</th></tr></thead>
		<tbody>
			{species.map((s) => (
				<tr data-region={s.region} data-type={s.types.join('|')} data-ability={[...s.abilityIds, s.hiddenAbilityId].filter(Boolean).join('|')} data-availability={availabilityToken(s)}>
					<td data-sort-value={s.baseSpeciesId}>{s.baseSpeciesId}{s.formId !== 0 && <span class="ability-summary small">Form {s.formId}</span>}</td>
					<td><div class="pokemon-cell"><PokemonImage s={s} /><a href={url(`/pokemon/${s.slug}/`)}>{s.name}</a>{s.game && <span class="sr-only"> {s.game}</span>}</div></td>
					<td>{s.types.map((t) => <Type type={t} />)}</td>
					<td>{s.abilityIds.map(id => <AbilityLink id={id} />)}</td>
					<td><AbilityLink id={s.hiddenAbilityId} /></td>
					<td class="base-stat">{s.stats.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0)}</td>
					{s.stats.map(value => <td class="base-stat">{value}</td>)}
					<td>{s.unavailableReason ? <Availability reason={s.unavailableReason} /> : hasDocumentedSource(s) ? 'Where to get it' : s.battleOnly ? 'Battle only' : 'No known way to get it'}</td>
				</tr>
			))}
		</tbody>
	</table>
</StarlightPage>

<style>
	.base-stat { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }
</style>
